findings:
- finding_id: I1
  title: Dependencies inline instead of workspace level
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added uuid and chrono as workspace dependencies but the reviewer flagged
    unused dependencies without mentioning inline version specifications. No phase
    caught the workspace = true issue for the 6 inline dependencies.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned FieldErrorCode or #[non_exhaustive] on any enum.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote tests checking trace_id exists in meta but did not assert it
    derives from request context. No phase flagged the hardcoded 'none' value.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] No observability despite tracing dependency'\
    \ \u2014 'Zero tracing::info!(), tracing::error!(), tracing::warn!(), or #[instrument]\
    \ attributes anywhere in the codebase. No structured logging on auth failures,\
    \ rate limit triggers, or request lifecycle.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified error messages are sanitized and noted no logging exists,
    but did not specifically flag that a SECURITY comment claims logging that doesn't
    exist.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test or review comment addresses non-ASCII characters in X-Tenant-ID
    header extraction.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests checking status codes and that no stack traces
    leak, but reviewer noted the verified check only confirms 'no stack traces, crate
    names, or internal details leak' without mentioning body content assertions. The
    tests check status code but the gap of missing body assertions was not flagged.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CORS tests in api_security.rs but no phase flagged that the
    test only checks status code without verifying CORS headers in the response.
- finding_id: I9
  title: "Wrong log levels \u2014 error! for 4xx client errors"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Since I4 (no logging at all) was caught but not fixed in this pipeline
    run, the wrong-log-level issue never had a chance to manifest.
- finding_id: I10
  title: CORS allows Any origin/method/header (CWE-942)
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CORS tests but no phase flagged that CorsLayer uses allow_origin(Any),
    allow_methods(Any), allow_headers(Any), which is CWE-942.
